# Context

## Background
T069 (review-fix-plan F5) connected scenario execution end to end:
shared gateway request path, behavior child bootstrap, state commit
and final snapshot in the runner, webclip's eight stateful operations,
and the scripted participant through the public run command.

## Why This Way
- AC-125 is marked partial, not covered: the happy path and the
  failing control are durable tests, while isolation (--count 2),
  seed determinism (same batch id in two workspaces), and injected
  backend failure rollback were proven live on 2026-09-15 through the
  oal bin only. The map keeps requires_live true.
- T074 records the replay gap: oal replay --verify rebuilds a
  stateless fixture gateway, so it cannot replay scenario batches
  (eight-of-nine mismatch on a healthy run). Fixing it needs a design
  decision on how frozen inputs reference the behavior module.
- The docs-claims test pins "Implemented components, not connected"
  in the README, so that heading stays; its list now names only the
  surfaces that are still unconnected (direct and catalog tools,
  study scheduler).

## Gotchas
- The quickstart scenario command writes .oal/runs/<batch> under the
  repository root; .gitignore covers .oal/ so demo batches leave no
  git noise. Verified live before committing the doc text.

